    "T4": {
      "category": "env_fault",
      "truth": "Environment not ready, not a design failure. scripts/env.local.sh sets PDK_ROOT=$HOME/pdk/ihp, which does not exist (the PDK is under ~/.ciel). Effects: the bypass case fails to build (Verilator: cannot find the IHP SRAM models under $PDK_ROOT/ihp-sg13g2/libs.ref/sg13g2_sram/verilog), env.sh itself prints 'IHP SRAM models: MISSING', and synthesis cannot read the liberty files. Fix: remove that line or point PDK_ROOT at ~/.ciel. The design itself passes bypass on a correct environment. Note: eda-agent's own setup diagnosis catches the synth stage (FATAL synth pdk) but reports the sim stage as 'environment ready' with a failed case; that is a known gap, not part of the truth.",
      "evidence": ["eval-f/_gt/T4_bypass.txt + regress/results/*/soc/bypass/verilator/verilator.log (4 x %Error: Cannot find file ... sg13g2_sram)", "eval-f/_gt/T4_doctor.txt (synth: ENVIRONMENT NOT READY, missing PDK_ROOT directory; sim: 'environment ready', 1 failed)"],
